{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. Summary:\n\n**Root cause:** `bucket_of` in `repo/histogram.py` returned `value // width` without clamping. A value on the top edge (`value == width * n_buckets`) produced index `n_buckets`, which is out of range — that's the IndexError on the last bucket, and it also skewed the chart (the top-edge count was being lost/raised instead of landing in the final bucket).\n\n**Fix:** clamp the computed index to `n_buckets - 1` when it overflows, matching the documented behavior:\n\n```python\ndef bucket_of(value, width, n_buckets):\n    \"\"\"...\"\"\"\n    index = value // width\n    if index >= n_buckets:\n        return n_buckets - 1\n    return index\n```\n\nBoth visible tests pass, and `histogram_summary` now correctly buckets top-edge values into the last bucket instead of erroring."}]},"session_id":"87e965bd-0d54-455c-aae5-a0fc7ce6f72f"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":32143,"duration_api_ms":32143,"is_error":false,"result":"The bug is clear. In `bucket_of`, a value on the top edge (`value == width * n_buckets`) returns `n_buckets`, which is out of range — that's the IndexError on the last bucket. The docstring even documents the intended clamp behavior.Now let me verify the fix against the tests:Both tests pass. Let me also confirm the downstream `histogram_summary` no longer errors on a top-edge value:Fixed. Summary:\n\n**Root cause:** `bucket_of` in `repo/histogram.py` returned `value // width` without clamping. A value on the top edge (`value == width * n_buckets`) produced index `n_buckets`, which is out of range — that's the IndexError on the last bucket, and it also skewed the chart (the top-edge count was being lost/raised instead of landing in the final bucket).\n\n**Fix:** clamp the computed index to `n_buckets - 1` when it overflows, matching the documented behavior:\n\n```python\ndef bucket_of(value, width, n_buckets):\n    \"\"\"...\"\"\"\n    index = value // width\n    if index >= n_buckets:\n        return n_buckets - 1\n    return index\n```\n\nBoth visible tests pass, and `histogram_summary` now correctly buckets top-edge values into the last bucket instead of erroring.","session_id":"87e965bd-0d54-455c-aae5-a0fc7ce6f72f","request_id":"a9acc7a0-2ca3-4e16-9a18-e7d4b8cc41a6","usage":{"inputTokens":19043,"outputTokens":1098,"cacheReadTokens":90688,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
